Steps:
[NAV] {{FRONT_URL}}
[WAIT] h1 visible in main
[SCROLL] to the footer

Assertions:
[DOM] footer text matches /^Ver\. 3\.\d+\.\d+/ (the Next theme, not vc-frontend 2.x) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] main h2 headings appear in this order: "Shop by category", "Popular with buyers", "Become a customer" (other sections may sit between them) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] header has searchbox "Search products and parts", links "Bulk order", "Compare", "Cart" and "Sign in" {OBSERVED}
[DOM] no Page Builder block markup in main: on Next "/" always renders the built-in home (KB-A788D882) {OBSERVED}
[NAV] link "Become a customer" in the last section points to /sign-up {OBSERVED}

Steps:
[NAV] {{FRONT_URL}}
[WAIT] h2 "Popular with buyers" visible
[WAIT] 5 s for the sections to load their content

Assertions:
[COUNT] "Shop by category" section shows >= 1 category link, each opening a page whose h1 equals the link text {SPEC}
[COUNT] "Popular with buyers" section shows >= 1 product card with a non-zero price {SPEC}
[REL] link "See all" opens a category page whose "products found" count is >= the number of cards in the section {SPEC}

[REL] page h1 == cat_name {OBSERVED}
[REL] last breadcrumb == cat_name, breadcrumbs start with "Home" {OBSERVED}
[FORMAT] text next to the h1 matches /^\d+ products? found$/ and the number is >= 1 {OBSERVED}

[DOM] dropdown has a "Products" group with >= 1 item, each item with a price {OBSERVED}
[NAV] URL is /search?q=<term> {OBSERVED}
[REL] with a "View all N results" button: "N products found" on /search == N; without it (every match fits the dropdown, KB-804C2453): "N products found" == d {SPEC}
[DOM] h1 contains the term {OBSERVED}

[DOM] h1 reads "Sorry, your search for "<term>" didn't return any results" with the exact term {OBSERVED}
[COUNT] 0 product cards in main {OBSERVED}
[DOM] "There are no results found" and a "Reset filters" button visible {OBSERVED}

[COUNT] exactly 4 sort tabs, in order "Featured", "Price ↑", "Price ↓", "Newest"; "Featured" pressed {SPEC}
[DOM] switches "Purchased before", "In stock", "Available at branches" in that order {OBSERVED}
[STATE] "In stock" is on, a "Show in stock" filter chip and a "Reset filters" button are shown {OBSERVED}
[DOM] "Switch to grid view" is pressed, "Switch to list view" is not {OBSERVED}

[NAV] after "Price ↑" the URL has sort=price-ascending {OBSERVED}
[DOM] after "Price ↑" the 12 prices are non-decreasing {SPEC}
[DOM] after "Price ↓" the 12 prices are non-increasing {SPEC}
[REL] the first price under "Price ↓" >= the last price under "Price ↑" {SPEC}

[REL] n_off >= n_on {SPEC}
[DOM] with In stock off the "Show in stock" chip is gone {OBSERVED}
[REL] with In stock on again the count == n_on and the "Show in stock" chip is back {SPEC}

[REL] number of product cards == n {SPEC}
[DOM] the last line of the grid reads "You have reached the end of the list." {OBSERVED}
[COUNT] no product title appears twice {SPEC}

[REL] "products found" count == n_brand and < n_all {SPEC}
[REL] every card's brand line == brand {SPEC}
[DOM] a filter chip naming brand is shown {SPEC}

[REL] h1 == p_title {OBSERVED}
[REL] "Price:" in "Price and delivery" == p_price, non-zero {SPEC}
[FORMAT] a SKU line matches /^SKU #\S+/ with a "Copy" button {OBSERVED}
[FORMAT] "In stock" shows a whole number >= 1 {OBSERVED}

[DOM] before a choice the price reads "N/A" and "Add to cart" is disabled with name "Select options to proceed" {OBSERVED}
